# tools/crypto_hybrid_identity_witness.rish — the HYBRID identity: one backup phrase grown into all THREE keys the transition years want — the classical
# Ed25519 signing key AND the two lattice keys a post-quantum identity carries (an ML-DSA signing key and an ML-KEM key-agreement key), authored in pure
# Rye. The safe-by-default identity the dual-key discovery named: during the years between "the curves are fine" and "a quantum computer broke the
# curves," the strongest identity carries BOTH families, so a break in either one still leaves the identity standing on the other. It composes only GREEN
# rungs (crypto/kumara_identity.rye the classical half, crypto/kumara_pq_identity.rye the post-quantum half), authoring no new cryptography (Season G).
#
# Season: crypto — the same mnemonic grows all three keys by two independent derivations (the classical through BIP-39 + SLIP-0010, the lattice keys
# through BIP-39 + HKDF domain separation), so a keeper reaches three independent keys with one remembered phrase. The hybrid signature carries both an
# Ed25519 and an ML-DSA signature and verifies iff BOTH verify, so a forger must break both families, not one.
# Design read: active-designing/20260816-192400_post-quantum-identity-is-dual-key.md ("hybrid, not either-or, is the safe default … a break in either
# family still leaves the identity standing on the other"). Clean-room: BIP-39, SLIP-0010, RFC 5869, FIPS 203/204 are public standards; the composition
# is our own Rye wiring over our own GREEN rungs, no line copied (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# crypto/hybrid_identity.rye is proven at every tier (small ML-DSA-44/ML-KEM-512, default ML-DSA-65/ML-KEM-768, large ML-DSA-87/ML-KEM-1024): no drift
# (the classical half equals kumara_identity's own from_mnemonic byte-for-byte, the post-quantum half equals kumara_pq_identity's own), three distinct
# keys (Ed25519 public, ML-DSA public, ML-KEM ek pairwise different), the hybrid signature requiring BOTH halves (a signature with only one family valid
# is rejected — a forger who breaks one family alone is caught), plus determinism and distinctness. Each half is proven one rung down. Purely local —
# no key held, no network, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/crypto_hybrid_identity_witness.rish

say "crypto-hybrid-identity: Language EN — the hybrid identity: one backup phrase grown into all three keys the transition years want, the classical Ed25519 key beside the two lattice keys a post-quantum identity carries. The safe default while both worlds overlap: a break in either family still leaves the identity standing on the other. It composes crypto/kumara_identity and crypto/kumara_pq_identity from the same mnemonic by two independent derivations, and offers a hybrid signature that verifies only when both the Ed25519 and the ML-DSA halves verify. Composes only GREEN rungs, authoring no new cryptography."
say "crypto-hybrid-identity: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively as a name that stands on both worlds at once: the forger held off by two families, the phrase remembered still only one. The three keys are independent key material drawn from one phrase; the hybrid signature is as strong as the stronger family and survives a break in either, because a forger must break both to be accepted."
say "crypto-hybrid-identity: Lens TAME — contract asserts (the three public keys distinct storage, both halves grown before returning), bounded loops, named-error composition from both identity doors. Proven at all three tiers with no fabricated constant: no drift from either composed door, three distinct keys, the hybrid signature requiring both halves (a valid-Ed25519/tampered-ML-DSA signature rejected, a valid-ML-DSA/tampered-Ed25519 signature rejected, a flipped message refused), and determinism plus distinctness. The module's own functions call no std.crypto — each half is proven one rung down. Every identity is a TEST identity from a published-vector mnemonic — no key held, no network, no funds, no device; a real hybrid identity from the maintainer's own phrase stays the custody gate, constant-time timing-safety the named horizon."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "crypto/bin/hybrid_identity"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p crypto/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build crypto/hybrid_identity.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "crypto-hybrid-identity: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "crypto/bin/hybrid_identity.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "crypto-hybrid-identity: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "crypto-hybrid-identity: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN crypto-hybrid-identity' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "crypto-hybrid-identity: selftest did not print the GREEN crypto-hybrid-identity line"
